maluos-firstboot (0.1.19) resolute; urgency=medium

  * role: application-server (docs/phase14-application-servers.md): the
    platform services (the tenant, the vault, the gateway, the memory face)
    and applications, no kernel and no MaluDB API of its own. After the
    components it joins the estate (enroll: kind estate, through maluctl
    estate join, without the overlay unless enroll.overlay) and installs
    application_server.apps through the kernel server's applications' door
    (maludb-os-core's install_remote_apps).
  * Two servers on one database server: an application server whose data is
    on a database server uses names of its own there, the database
    maludb_<suffix> and the roles maluos-vault-<suffix>, -gateway-, -memory-
    (platform_suffix, platform_db, db_role; database_server.suffix or the
    host's name). A kernel server and a single host keep the plain names.
  * The summary carries role, application_server and platform_suffix.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

maluos-firstboot (0.1.18) resolute; urgency=medium

  * maluctl db export names the database server by a name the other
    servers' own network resolves and its certificate carries (the first of
    database_server.names, else the host's full name), not the overlay name:
    an office cannot reach its own database over the overlay at first boot
    (the owner's answer 2026-11-12: the LAN name). The listener's URL the
    same.

